From k35: routed engines, Handler::Passthrough and A2A/ACP timeouts lose their category at await: non-stream → generic 500, mid-stream → '[error: …]' text chunk in _handle_stream. Carry a typed error (e.g. failure category 'timeout' from Net::Async::HTTP / core k278) through the handler chain and map to 504 + the protocol's error frame, mirroring the raw passthrough path. Tests native + PSGI.
